land-atlas/kansas/osborne-county"],["ARC or PLC in Osborne County","/arc-plc/kansas/osborne-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids. November to December came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those years, the most of any pair, and April to May did it in 33. In 2025, February to March came in at 32% of normal on the middle, and so far in 2026 June to July is at 152%. Grid 23227 had its driest year in 1956 at 47% of normal.</p>"}
